<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60332" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κτέρ-εα</span></b> , τά (no sg. in
		use), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>funeral gifts</i>, burnt
			with the dead, <i><span class="en">
				Mosch.
				4.33
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>: generally, <i>funeral honours</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ κτέρεα κτερεΐξαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					1.291
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				2.222
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.38
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλαχον κτερέων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					5.311
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ὁσίων ἀντίασεν κτερέων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
					514
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Maced.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> later,
				<i>wrappers for the dead, shroud</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνὶ κτερέεσσιν ἐλυσθείς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.254
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
